		<p>Lilly, being a shorter-haired dog, tends to be chilly when Ella wants shade. No worries;
		the deck on which we have the shower catches the morning sun.</p>
		
		<p>On our 28 acres, Ella and Lilly have free reign. However, they always stay close
		to the cabin if either Keith or I is there. When I ride the quad up to Zach's level,
		Lilly almost always runs ahead of me; she seems to be playing that I am chasing her.
		Ella sometimes runs up with us, but as often she just hangs out in the cabin.</p>
		
		<p>But when we are both working, say at the solar shed, they'll come along and relax.
		It would seem that the underside of the shed deck is just like a crate to Ella.</p>
		
		<img src="20200811_174918.jpg">
		<img src="20200811_174921.jpg">
